<div class="frido-faq__qa">
  <h3 class="frido-faq__question">Does Frido footwear help with neuropathy?</h3>
  <div class="frido-faq__answer">
    <p>Yes. Frido footwear is designed with features that support individuals suffering from neuropathy, such as a wide toe box, non-binding upper, slip-resistant sole, and flat, flexible design to encourage better circulation and reduce pressure on sensitive nerves.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="frido-faq__qa">
  <h3 class="frido-faq__question">Is Frido footwear good for plantar fasciitis?</h3>
  <div class="frido-faq__answer">
    <p>Yes. Frido’s ergonomic design helps reduce pressure on the heel and plantar fascia, supports proper arch alignment, and promotes natural movement, which is beneficial for plantar fasciitis sufferers.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="frido-faq__qa">
  <h3 class="frido-faq__question">Does Frido footwear have arch support?</h3>
  <div class="frido-faq__answer">
    <p>The shoes embrace a barefoot philosophy with a minimalist sole and no built-in arch support. Optional orthopedic insoles are available separately.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="frido-faq__qa">
  <h3 class="frido-faq__question">Does Frido footwear run true to size?</h3>
  <div class="frido-faq__answer">
    <p>Yes, most users find that Frido footwear runs true to size. For those with wider feet or orthotic needs, a size guide is available on the website, and half-size adjustments are recommended when in doubt.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="frido-faq__qa">
  <h3 class="frido-faq__question">Are you supposed to wear socks with Frido footwear?</h3>
  <div class="frido-faq__answer">
    <p>You can wear them with or without socks, depending on your preference. The interior is designed to be comfortable and breathable even without socks, but wearing moisture-wicking socks may enhance hygiene and fit for some users.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="frido-faq__qa">
  <h3 class="frido-faq__question">What are the materials used in your shoes?</h3>
  <div class="frido-faq__answer">
    <p>Our barefoot shoes are crafted with precision and the highest-quality materials to ensure comfort and performance. Here are the key materials used in our footwear:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Upper Material:</strong> We use premium polyester for the upper part of our barefoot shoes. This material provides durability and a comfortable fit.</li>
      <li><strong>Sole Material:</strong> The sole of our shoes is made from organic rubber, offering excellent grip and flexibility.</li>
      <li><strong>Winter Shoes:</strong> Our winter variants feature the same organic rubber sole for traction, but the inside is lined with a special insole material that combines EVA and cotton wool. This provides extra insulation and warmth during colder seasons.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="frido-faq__qa">
  <h3 class="frido-faq__question">Is Frido footwear washable?</h3>
  <div class="frido-faq__answer">
    <p>Yes. Most Frido models are surface-washable using a damp cloth. For deeper cleaning, remove the insole and hand-wash gently with mild soap and water. You can also machine wash your shoes by selecting the delicate or gentle cycle.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="frido-faq__qa">
  <h3 class="frido-faq__question">How to clean Frido footwear?</h3>
  <div class="frido-faq__answer">
    <p>Use a soft cloth or sponge with mild soap to spot-clean. Remove insoles if needed.</p>
  </div>
</div>

